		{"id":"ee6223b13224ae19","type":"group","x":1960,"y":-2620,"width":880,"height":220,"color":"2","label":"Phase 1"},
		{"id":"f2af0d77aa8030c4","type":"group","x":2060,"y":-1260,"width":415,"height":226,"color":"5","label":"Phase 3"},
		{"id":"c33710328216adb0","type":"group","x":2925,"y":-4380,"width":300,"height":220,"label":"Datasets"},
		{"id":"5ccc582e9a327a72","type":"group","x":5035,"y":-1080,"width":300,"height":190,"label":"NATIVE"},
		{"id":"307d725d4afc9ece","type":"group","x":-1292,"y":-2280,"width":2345,"height":1303,"color":"2","label":"Nuscenes"},
		{"id":"2d6ee5647020e53f","type":"group","x":-1292,"y":-873,"width":1952,"height":893,"color":"4","label":"Kradar"},
		{"id":"aabf884dad8fc1e2","type":"group","x":6100,"y":-3440,"width":1760,"height":450,"label":"Untitled group"},
		{"id":"ea3bb3c169584a14","type":"group","x":6140,"y":-1840,"width":440,"height":400,"label":"pipelines/pipeline_detection_v1_0.py"},
		{"id":"5d32f2d270944c89","type":"group","x":2925,"y":-4720,"width":300,"height":220,"label":"Models"},
		{"id":"9823525092e32840","type":"file","file":"Images/Pasted image 20260323134322.png","x":-392,"y":-1360,"width":400,"height":186},
		{"id":"669b657cab31d33a","type":"text","text":"kradar","x":-365,"y":-540,"width":106,"height":60,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"fb961577459c2561","type":"file","file":"Images/Pasted image 20260323104358.png","x":-365,"y":-260,"width":400,"height":260},
		{"id":"6b07d3a2cdb74873","type":"text","text":"1. Using established methods for sensor-specific encoders and detection head for extracting BEV feature maps\n2. Main novelty is that for each patch the best sensor is given weightage and using a weighted average of all three sensors the unified bev map is generated\n3. ASF dynamically adapts to different sensor combinations without retraining","x":240,"y":-619,"width":400,"height":289},
		{"id":"38f84d7c7807a473","type":"text","text":"NOTES:\n1. The main disadvantage of camera only modality is lack of depth info","x":685,"y":-851,"width":348,"height":201,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"b200c1f22390bd14","type":"file","file":"Images/Pasted image 20260323135145.png","x":603,"y":-1237,"width":399,"height":246},
		{"id":"cc753e1cb3c71aab","type":"text","text":"nuscenes","x":-84,"y":-1680,"width":122,"height":60,"color":"2"},
		{
			"id":"cbb8158b72cb1d94",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"MVP",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"x":-387,
			"y":-1820,
			"width":250,
			"height":60,
			"color":"2"
		},
		{"id":"7b544587e79e0179","type":"file","file":"Images/Pasted image 20260323131940.png","x":-387,"y":-2254,"width":400,"height":348},
		{"id":"1417ad984497c2b4","type":"text","text":"1. Individual backbones and detection heads for camera and lidar where feature maps and bounding boxes are generated.\n2. Using these queries are generated which is fed to an encoder.\n3. Self-attention and cross-attention for generating *detections*. (Not BEV Maps but BEV maps can be inferred)\n4. It is faster than BEVFusion during inference","x":213,"y":-2160,"width":515,"height":240},
		{"id":"5f55217fc997de6c","type":"text","text":"1. Camera still needs more work especially during adverse weather.\n2. Camera feature map is not well integrated with the rest","x":-115,"y":-650,"width":300,"height":161,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"ae7d0ffc1cc283dd","type":"text","text":"EA-LSS","x":-512,"y":-1513,"width":250,"height":60,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"52f19bd38eb7f831","type":"text","text":"[Availability-Aware](https://github.com/kaist-avelab/K-Radar)","x":-90,"y":-390,"width":195,"height":60,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"11cdfc52a573e0cb","type":"text","text":"Echofusion","x":-660,"y":-390,"width":134,"height":60,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"427fb5321fcf2ce6","type":"text","text":"1. Uses seperate backbones to extract multi-level features from RT(Range-Time) radar maps and images.\n2. No heavy processing of Radar data; so has access to relatively dense radar cloud\n3. Cross attention -\n\t1. “This azimuth corresponds to exactly one image column.”\n\t2. “This range corresponds to a specific row in the RT map.”","x":-1160,"y":-853,"width":450,"height":283},
		{"id":"2d0a7b3c08170a41","type":"text","text":"1. Performs better for long range detection than short range detection due to liberal annotations in long range\n2. Imperfect Z localization - blaming LiDAR annotation","x":-1272,"y":-434,"width":432,"height":174,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"dae158106eb5cc47","type":"text","text":"1. Adds EADF and FDG as additions to LSS for improving loss calculation; for solving Depth Jump.","x":-892,"y":-1416,"width":317,"height":149},
		{"id":"f0c2a9f07413882b","type":"text","text":"Depth Jump: When a camera-only model tries to predict depth for every pixel in an image (the first step of LSS), it often makes sudden, incorrect jumps exactly at the edges of objects.","x":-872,"y":-1651,"width":277,"height":198},
		{"id":"59cc9ade8ca92034","type":"file","file":"Images/Pasted image 20260323110827.png","x":-960,"y":-181,"width":400,"height":181},
		{"id":"31587cb1e6835bdf","type":"text","text":"1. Generates segmentation mask for object and generates LiDAR points frustum.\n2. Random points are sampled inside the mask and using the closes LiDAR point depth is given to the sampled point. Then projected to 3D.\n3. Main reason they do this is because LiDAR cant detect far away objects and this creates virtual points.","x":-1032,"y":-2214,"width":402,"height":254},
		{"id":"425a0489c288673e","type":"text","text":"FDG: Make the DepthNet focus computational capacity on actual object surfaces instead of empty sky/road.","x":-1272,"y":-1340,"width":290,"height":120},
		{"id":"1d0200ea15f54141","type":"text","text":"EADF: Force the depth map to respect sharp discontinuities at object edges instead of blurring them.","x":-1272,"y":-1483,"width":290,"height":120},
		{"id":"268a555de6418bcb","type":"text","text":"1. Virtual points are assumed to have same depth as close by Lidar measurements. Which is not always true.","x":-1032,"y":-1844,"width":438,"height":109,"color":"1"},
